   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1945-09-22">September 22, 1945</date></dateline>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3284" type="person">Fred</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>I have received a copy of my paper and the other material concerning the Religion and
               Health Seminar. I have noticed a very grave omission of the typewritten copy and I
               ask you to send a postcard or a letter to all those who have received a copy of my
               paper, containing the following statement:</p>
            <p>"In the paper of <rs type="person" ref="#tillich_person_id__1928">Dr. Tillich</rs> on
               page 17, before the first paragraph (a few sweeping .......) the following must be
               inserted:<lb/> c) <hi rend="u">Man as dynamic unity or static composite</hi></p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Looking forward to seeing you soon. Cordially yours,</salute>
               <signed><rs type="person" ref="#tillich_person_id__1928">Paul Tillich</rs></signed>
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
